AU  - Mingqian Li
AU  - Sina Zadeh
AU  - Raymundo Arroyave
AU  - Xiaoning Qian
PY  - 2026
T2  - Proceedings of the International Conference on Machine Learning (ICML 2026)
AB  - In batch multi-objective Bayesian optimization (MOBO), it is often desirable to identify the whole Pareto optimal set, especially when considering the complicated interplay between different design criteria and constraints. This poses unique challenges in acquiring batches of both high quality and diversity to cover the Pareto front. We propose a novel acquisition strategy, Probability of Matching (POM), which evaluates both batch candidate quality and diversity by explicitly capturing the likelihood that all batch points are Pareto optimal, and the probability that they collectively cover the full Pareto set. To estimate the coverage probability and promote diversity, we incorporate non-replacement sampling principles, resulting in our new POM-guided batch MOBO method. Across synthetic benchmarks and real-world tasks, our method consistently outperforms state-of-the-art baselines on standard MOBO metrics as well as a new design-space coverage metric, Expected Minimum Distance (EMD), with comparable computational efficiency.
